# Register write-lock journal (scripts/register-lock.sh) — LIVE session state,
# never committed: it records who had which shared register path open, and a
# committed copy would be another actor's stale state in your tree. Pulling
# someone else's open ACQUIRE rows would make YOUR `acquire` refuse paths nobody
# holds. That reason is about the live half only.
# The EVIDENCE half IS tracked, at docs/loop/register-locks-archive/<date>.tsv —
# written by `register-lock.sh archive`, read by nobody as live state, and the
# durable answer to GOALS-SCORECARD G1-C5. See that script's do_archive comment.
.register-locks*
